       "type": "tip",
-      "content": "Notice how the gerund can sit right next to the subject with commas on both sides (San Martín, *renunciando*..., *se retiró*) — this reads almost like an aside, adding a second fact about the subject without making it the main point of the sentence."
+      "content": "The gerund has the same subject as the main verb: *Bolívar avanzó venciendo* means Bolívar did both. The tense comes from the main verb only."
     }
   ]
 }
diff --git a/content/es-latam/grammar/b1/b1-independencia-04-republicas-gr.json b/content/es-latam/grammar/b1/b1-independencia-04-republicas-gr.json
