   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "content": "A synthesis on who did and didn't benefit from independence needs passive voice constantly: a principle was proclaimed, a law was passed, a protection was eliminated, a right was not granted. These sentences are taken directly from the previous reading."
+      "content": "You know *aunque* and *a pesar de que* from A2 Unit 28: they admit a fact that goes against what follows. With a real fact, use the indicative. This pattern is useful when you compare what the constitutions said with what happened."
     },
     {
       "type": "examples",
       "items": [
         {
