 {
   "id": "grammar.b1.razaclasepoder.01.jerarquia",
-  "title": "Se pasiva / impersonal: la sociedad de castas",
+  "title": "Impersonal se: classifying people",
   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "content": "The se-passive fits classification systems well: people were classified, privileges were granted or denied, a genre became popular — all sustained social practices, not one official's single act. These sentences are taken directly from the previous reading."
+      "content": "You know *se* with a verb from B1 Unit 6: it says what is done without saying who does it. Here it describes how a whole society was organised. With a person as the object, the verb stays singular and takes the personal *a* (*se clasificaba a las personas*). With a thing, the verb agrees with it (*se pintaban las ropas*)."
     },
     {
       "type": "examples",
       "items": [
         {
-          "spanish": "En la sociedad colonial se clasificaba a las personas según su origen y su ascendencia.",
-          "english": "In colonial society, people were classified according to their origin and ancestry."
+          "spanish": "Se llamaba mestizo a una persona de origen español e indígena.",
+          "english": "A person of Spanish and indigenous origin was called a mestizo."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Con estas categorías se concedían, o se negaban, ciertos privilegios legales.",
-          "english": "With these categories, certain legal privileges were granted, or denied."
+          "spanish": "En los registros de bautizos se anotaba el origen de cada familia.",
+          "english": "In the baptism registers, the origin of each family was written down."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "En el siglo dieciocho, se popularizó en Nueva España un género pictórico dedicado a este sistema.",
-          "english": "In the eighteenth century, a pictorial genre devoted to this system became popular in New Spain."
+          "spanish": "En los cuadros se pintaban la ropa y los oficios de cada casta.",
+          "english": "In the paintings, the clothes and trades of each casta were painted."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Estas pinturas se encargaban a artistas locales, y se enviaban con frecuencia a España.",
-          "english": "These paintings were commissioned from local artists, and were frequently sent to Spain."
+          "spanish": "En el siglo XVIII se hacían series de pinturas de castas.",
+          "english": "In the 18th century, series of casta paintings were made."
         }
       ]
     },
     {
       "type": "tip",
-      "content": "Se clasificaba, se concedían, se encargaban — all imperfect tense, because these were ongoing, repeated practices, not single completed events. Watch how the se-passive verb agrees with what follows it: se concedían privilegios (plural verb for plural privilegios), se popularizó un género (singular verb for singular género)."
+      "content": "The imperfect (*se clasificaba*) fits a practice that went on for years; the preterite (*se hizo popular*) fits one change. Check the noun: *se anotaba el origen* (singular), *se pintaban los oficios* (plural), but with a person, *se clasificaba a las personas* stays singular."
     }
   ]
 }
diff --git a/content/es-latam/grammar/b1/b1-razaclasepoder-02-elites-gr.json b/content/es-latam/grammar/b1/b1-razaclasepoder-02-elites-gr.json
