diff --git a/content/es-latam/grammar/b1/b1-razaclasepoder-05-legados-gr.json b/content/es-latam/grammar/b1/b1-razaclasepoder-05-legados-gr.json
index 595cb937..6fa0d19a 100644
--- a/content/es-latam/grammar/b1/b1-razaclasepoder-05-legados-gr.json
+++ b/content/es-latam/grammar/b1/b1-razaclasepoder-05-legados-gr.json
@@ -1,35 +1,35 @@
 {
   "id": "grammar.b1.razaclasepoder.05.legados",
-  "title": "Voz pasiva: herencias de la jerarquía colonial",
+  "title": "Imperfect and present perfect: what has changed",
   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "content": "A synthesis on legacy needs passive voice to separate what changed legally (a law was abolished, a distinction was eliminated) from what didn't change as fast (structures were maintained, inherited, transformed rather than erased). These sentences are taken directly from the previous reading."
+      "content": "You know the imperfect (A2 Unit 21) and the present perfect (A2 Unit 1), and you met their contrast for change over time in B1 Unit 5. Use the imperfect for how things used to be in the colony, and the present perfect for what has changed since then and still matters now."
     },
     {
       "type": "examples",
       "items": [
         {
-          "spanish": "El sistema legal de castas fue abolido con notable rapidez tras las guerras de independencia.",
-          "english": "The legal caste system was abolished with notable speed after the wars of independence."
+          "spanish": "En 1800 la ley distinguía a las personas por su origen; desde entonces esa regla ha cambiado.",
+          "english": "In 1800 the law distinguished people by origin; since then that rule has changed."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Las distinciones legales basadas en el origen racial fueron eliminadas de la legislación en apenas unos años.",
-          "english": "Legal distinctions based on racial origin were eliminated from legislation within just a few years."
+          "spanish": "La tierra estaba en pocas manos, y la desigualdad no ha desaparecido.",
+          "english": "Land was in few hands, and inequality has not disappeared."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Las jerarquías no fueron simplemente borradas por un decreto legal: fueron transformadas, y en gran medida heredadas.",
-          "english": "The hierarchies were not simply erased by a legal decree: they were transformed, and largely inherited."
+          "spanish": "Antes muchos pueblos indígenas no tenían voz política; en las últimas décadas han ganado más derechos.",
+          "english": "Before, many indigenous peoples had no political voice; in recent decades they have gained more rights."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Ciertas prácticas culturales fueron mantenidas de forma casi inalterada durante décadas.",
-          "english": "Certain cultural practices were maintained almost unchanged for decades."
+          "spanish": "Los prejuicios eran fuertes en esa época, y todavía no han desaparecido por completo.",
+          "english": "Prejudices were strong at that time, and they have still not completely disappeared."
         }
       ]
     },
     {
       "type": "tip",
-      "content": "Fue abolido / fueron eliminadas mark a clean, dated legal event; fueron transformadas / fueron heredadas / fueron mantenidas describe something slower and less complete. Putting both kinds of passive sentence in the same paragraph is exactly how you argue that a law changing fast doesn't mean a society changed just as fast."
+      "content": "Words like *antes* and *en esa época* point to the imperfect; *desde entonces*, *todavía* and *en las últimas décadas* point to the present perfect, because the result is still true now."
